From d065c92f7e7ac4a6e4c1c9d50707fd8197e329cd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Latorrey Whitehead <torreyw94@tsmatter.com>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 17:29:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(demo): add Insurance demo spec + fix(insurance): wire up
 dead loadSample()

Bug fix (insurance-war-room.html):
- loadSample() and its SAMPLES object (claims/dme/policy) existed with
  a fully-defined .sample-chip CSS class, but no button anywhere in
  the DOM ever called it -- dead code, same pattern as other
  orphaned-feature findings across this repo. Wired up 3 real
  sample-chip buttons (#smp-claims/#smp-dme/#smp-policy) next to the
  paste textarea, matching the FinOps/Construction demo-sample
  pattern.

Demo spec (insurance-demo.json + insurance-demo.spec.js):
- Follows the healthcare-demo.json/spec.js pattern: war room load
  sample claims report -> fire 6 engines -> escalate to strategist ->
  run strategist chain -> escalate to executive portal -> KPIs +
  explainability panel.
- Selectors read directly from insurance-war-room.html /
  insurance-strategist.html / insurance-executive-portal.html (ids,
  onclick handlers, functions) -- NOT live-verified via Playwright,
  since this sandbox hits the same chrome-headless-shell 403 as the
  Codespace. Flagged in the spec's own note field; should be run once
  in Codespaces to confirm before treating as final.
